  "prefLabel": "Rev 1905.08 Remittances to the Treasurer by the Tax Collector",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rev 1905.08 Remittances to the Treasurer by the Tax Collector.\n\n(a) When making remittances to the treasurer, the tax collector shall complete a remittance advice containing the following information by year of levy and by type of tax:\n\n(1) The total amount of the principal of taxes;\n\n(2) Cost and expenses;\n\n(3) Interest; and\n\n(4) Penalties.\n\n(b) When making remittances to the treasurer covering tax redemption, the tax collector shall complete a separate remittance advice which shall contain the following information by year of levy:\n\n(1) Total amount of taxes being redeemed;\n\n(2) Total costs and expenses collected; and\n\n(3) Interest.\n\nSource. #8599, eff 4-6-06; ss by #10582, eff 5-2-14; ss by #13918, eff 3-29-24 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Rev 1900)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rev1900.html"
